WEBVTT

NOTE
Optional explanatory captions; this film has no spoken narration.
Architecture walkthrough with an illustrative task and controlled synthetic tests.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
A new session can repeat a solved bug
when the lesson is not retrieved.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Claude: custom prompt recall.
Codex: explicit recall tools and rules.

3
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Search relevant notes, vault and memories.
Treat source-linked matches as leads.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Open the source; check the correction,
its evidence and its scope.

5
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Here, a fresh key on every retry
creates a second operation identity.

6
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Reuse one key for the same operation.
The example server enforces uniqueness.

7
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Same key + UNIQUE + upsert: one stored row
in the controlled SQLite test.

8
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Capture hooks queue session evidence.
A worker processes the transcript later.

9
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:22.000
Proposed PR #8 preserves richer evidence.
Keep verified outcomes apart from proposals.

10
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Keep source-linked corrections.
Attribution does not establish approval.

11
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:41.000
The note is the source; QMD is its index.
Update text; embed vectors separately.

12
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Save the fix for the next task.
Recall → verify → act → capture → correct.
